ying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"NETGEAR, Inc. provides networking technologies for businesses, homes, and service providers in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. The company operates in two segments, Enterprise and Consumer. It offers Wi-Fi routers and home Wi-Fi mesh systems, Wi-Fi hotspots, broadband modems, Wi-Fi gateways, Wi-Fi range extenders, powerline adapters, and Wi-Fi network adapters; and provides value-added service offerings, including security and privacy, technical support, and parental controls. The company also provides pro AV Solutions, which includes Ethernet switches and WiFi access points; NETGEAR Engage Controller, a software that provides centralized, profile-based configuration, and unified management; NETGEAR Insight Remote Management; Pro Routers; enterprise-grade cloud managed or standalone access points; general purpose ethernet switches; and NETGEAR Exium Security Solutions, a security software that provides on-premises next-generation firewall and cloud-based secure access service edge. It markets and sells its products through wholesale distributors, traditional and online retailers, direct market resellers, value-added resellers, managed service provider, and broadband service providers, as well as through its direct online store. NETGEAR, Inc. was incorporated in 1996 and is headquartered in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Charles J. Prober | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 784 people. Revenue per employee of $892K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers. Stock-based compensation of $38K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["NETGEAR, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $512M market cap on $700M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -9% over the past three years and -6% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -10% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 30%.","The company is burning through $19M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 9.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 68/100): roic below cost of capital; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 237% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (NTGR) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/149/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_NTGR_Movement_110926082802_1794230882.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794230882.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding NETGEAR (NTGR) Reliance on International Revenue","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3026279/understanding-netgear-ntgr-reliance-on-international-revenue?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm_international_revenues-3026279","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794230103.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"NETGEAR (NTGR) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/netgear-ntgr-q3-2026-earnings-164328000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793897621.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"NETGEAR (NASDAQ:NTGR) Issues Quarterly Earnings Results, Beats Estimates By $0.18 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/netgear-nasdaqntgr-issues-quarterly-earnings-results-beats-estimates-by-0-18-eps.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793886050.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.103,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","legal"]},{"title":"Netgear outline